############################################################
# .gitignore
#
# Two categories of things must never land in git history:
#   1. The bundle payload — it is multi-GB of container image
#      tarballs and RPMs. It belongs on an artifact store or a
#      USB drive carried across the air gap, never in a git repo.
#   2. Cluster credentials — a kubeconfig is a cluster-admin
#      bearer credential. terraform.tfvars holds real node IPs
#      and (potentially) an SSH key path; state files can hold
#      rendered kubeadm configs with the bootstrap token and
#      certificate-key in plaintext.
############################################################

# --- bundle payload (requirement #14) ---
bundle/images/
bundle/rpms/
bundle/manifests/
bundle/bin/
bundle/.bundle-version
.artifacts/

# --- Terraform state & credentials ---
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars
kubeconfig-*
*.kubeconfig
crash.log
crash.*.log

# --- SSH material, just in case one gets dropped here ---
*.pem
id_rsa
id_ed25519

# --- editor / OS noise ---
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
